WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.569
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.569 --> 00:00:07.189
Here you see people that don’t exist.

00:00:07.189 --> 00:00:11.889
They don’t exist because these images were
created with a neural network-based learning

00:00:11.889 --> 00:00:17.970
method by the name StyleGAN2, which can not
only create eye-poppingly detailed looking

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:25.240
images, but it can also fuse these people
together, or generate cars, churches, horses,

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.620
and of course, cats.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:32.680
This is quite convincing so is there anything
else to do in human face generation?

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.149
Are we done?

00:00:34.149 --> 00:00:38.789
Well, this footage from a new paper may give
some of it away.

00:00:38.789 --> 00:00:43.249
If you have been watching this series for
a while, you know that of course, researchers

00:00:43.249 --> 00:00:48.579
always find a way to make these techniques
better, we always say, two more papers down

00:00:48.579 --> 00:00:51.949
the line and it will be way better.

00:00:51.949 --> 00:00:56.760
And now, we are one more paper down the line,
so let’s see together if there has been

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.059
any improvement.

00:00:58.059 --> 00:01:04.330
This new technique is based on StyleGAN2 and
is called StyleFlow, and it can take an input

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:09.160
photo of a test subject, and edit a number
of meaningful parameters.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:14.030
Age, expression, lighting, pose, you name
it.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:19.150
Now note that there were other techniques
that could pull this off, but the key improvements

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:26.750
here is that one, we can perform many sequential
changes, and two, is does all this while remaining

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:29.360
faithful to the original photo.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:35.340
And hold on to your papers, because three,
it can also help Elon Musk to grow a majestic

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:36.940
beard.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:41.500
Believe it or not, you will also see a run
of this algorithm on me as well at the end

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:42.500
of the video.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:52.090
First, let’s adjust the lighting a little,
and now, it’s time for that beard.

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:53.090
Loving it.

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:57.980
Now, a little aging, and one more beard.

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:04.640
It seems to me that this beard is different
from the young man beard, which is nice attention

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.060
to detail.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:10.969
And note that we have strayed very far from
the input image, but if you look at the intermediate

00:02:10.969 --> 00:02:16.030
states, you see that the essence of the test
subject is indeed quite similar.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:19.489
This Elon is still Elon.

00:02:19.489 --> 00:02:24.519
Note that these results are not publicly available
and were made specifically for us, so you

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:27.920
can only see this here on Two Minute Papers.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:32.700
That is quite an honor, so thank you very
much to Rameen Abdal, the first author of

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.959
the paper for being so kind.

00:02:34.959 --> 00:02:40.370
Now, another key improvement in this work
is that we can change one of these parameters

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:43.090
with little effect on anything else.

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:48.349
Have a look at this workflow and see how well
we can perform these sequential edits.

00:02:48.349 --> 00:02:53.090
These are the source images, and the labels
showcase the one variable change for each

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:58.700
subsequent image, and you can see how amazingly
surgical the changes are.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:02:59.700
Witchcraft.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:05.190
If it says that we change the facial hair,
that’s the only change I see in the output.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:10.959
And just think about the fact that these starting
images are real photos, but the outputs of

00:03:10.959 --> 00:03:14.799
the algorithm are made-up people that don’t
exist.

00:03:14.799 --> 00:03:20.060
And notice that the background is also mostly
left untouched.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.359
Why does that matter?

00:03:21.359 --> 00:03:23.940
You will see in the next example.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:28.029
So far, so good, but this method can do way
more than this.

00:03:28.029 --> 00:03:31.930
Now let’s edit, not people, but cars.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:40.230
I love how well the color and pose variations
work.

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:49.359
Now, if you look here, you see that there
is quite a bit of collateral damage, as not

00:03:49.359 --> 00:03:54.669
only the cars, but the background is also
changing, opening up the door for a potentially

00:03:54.669 --> 00:03:57.469
more surgical followup paper.

00:03:57.469 --> 00:04:02.170
Make sure to subscribe and hit the bell icon
to get notified when we cover this one more

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.079
paper down the line.

00:04:04.079 --> 00:04:08.599
And now, here is what you have been waiting
for, we’ll get hands-on experience with

00:04:08.599 --> 00:04:13.060
this technique, where I shall be the subject
of the next experiment.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:18.940
First, the algorithm is looking for high-resolution
frontal images, so for instance, this would

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:22.430
not work at all, we would have to look for
a different image.

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:28.030
No matter, here’s another one where I got
locked up for reading too many papers.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:33.080
This could be used as an input for the algorithm,
and, look.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.940
This image looks a little different.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:36.949
Why is that?

00:04:36.949 --> 00:04:42.340
It is because StyleGAN2 runs an embedding
operation on the photo before starting its

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.340
work.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:48.680
This is an interesting detail that we only
see if we start using the technique ourselves.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:52.330
And now, come on, give me that beard.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:53.919
Ho-ho-hoo!

00:04:53.919 --> 00:04:54.919
Loving it!

00:04:54.919 --> 00:04:58.620
What do you think, whose beard is better,
Elon’s or mine?

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:00.620
Let me know in the comments below.

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:05.610
And now, please meet old man Károly, he will
tell you that papers were way better back

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:09.590
in his day, and the usual transformations.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:16.330
But also note that as a limitation, we had
quite a bit of collateral damage for the background.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.520
This was quite an experience.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:20.050
Thank you so much.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:23.889
And we are not done yet because this paper
just keeps on giving.

00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:26.670
It can also perform attribute transfer.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:31.530
What this means is that we have two input
photos, this will be the source image, and

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:35.879
we can choose a bunch of parameters that we
would like to extract from it.

00:05:35.879 --> 00:05:41.090
For instance, the lighting and pose can be
extracted through attribute transfer, and

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:46.740
it seems to even estimate the age of the target
subject and change the source to match it

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.220
better.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:49.220
Loving it.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:52.940
The source code for this technique is also
available and make sure to have a look at

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:59.000
the paper, it is very thoroughly evaluated,
the authors went the extra mile there and

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.490
it really shows.

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:05.480
And I hope that you now agree, even if there
is a technique that appears quite mature,

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:09.330
researchers always find a way to further improve
it.

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:14.010
And who knew, it took a competent AI to get
me to grow a beard.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:15.550
Totally worth it.

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:33.050
What 

00:06:33.050 --> 00:07:10.530
a time 

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:20.270
to be alive!

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:23.580
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

